WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:06.810
Original Translations: Lunar, Ayu, AnimeYuki-Spork 
 Encode: Jumonji-Giri 
 Other work: ReDone-Subs

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.600
Misae, we're home.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.250
Nao-chan, the bath will be ready soon,
 so get yourself out of those clothes.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.430
Yeah, if you don't hurry, 
you might catch a cold.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.110
I'll take{carry} this young lady to the tatami room.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:32.740
Get changed quickly and come back down.
 I've already made tea.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.080
Your phone call came out of nowhere and took me by surprise.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.890
{Yo. You were slow. }What took you so long, slowpoke?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.690
Iriya's Sky {not gonna do 2 separate moves with this, I'm already lagging my own system enough with this TS}

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.690
Summer of UFOs

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.080
Iriya's Sky, Summer of UFOs

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.370
Hey, Mom.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.370
Hmm?

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.820
Is something going on tomorrow? {happening}

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.270
Eh? I thought it was a school day.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.580
Did Onii-chan circle it?

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.230
Ah, I bet you're hungry, Principal.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.280
Honey, where's Naoyuki? {what's he doing}

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.680
Same place as usual. {same thing as always -- try to take over the world}

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.400
Ever since he got back, he's been 
holed up in his room almost all the time.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.200
Dear, won't you go and talk to him?

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.400
Sure. I suppose it's already been three days.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.180
<i>In three days. {138} {It's like The Ring, only 4 days fewer.}</i>

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.000
Huh? What's that?

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.480
It's green ramen. It has chlorella in it.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.440
I guess the world is full of wonders.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.610
Oh, the day after you eat this, your poop will turn green. {fsc}

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.100
Is it good?

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.620
It's good enough. {pretty tasty / normal-average}

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.180
Hmm, not bad.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.110
So where's Iriya now?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.660
She's passed out in the van 
parked in front of the house. {passed out?}

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:26.020
I'm surprised she's managed to live this long.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.390
If that's the case, 
why didn't you retrieve her earlier!? {make your move}

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.670
I'm gonna tell you the truth.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.200
I wasn't planning on seriously searching for you guys. {no intention of seriously searching}{didn't seriouly plan to go after}

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.640
What do you mean?

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.440
Exactly what I said.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.020
I figured I'd let Iriya spend her
 remaining time alone with you,{I thought that Iriya spending the time she had left to live with you...} {rw} {that if Ir could be with u in her remaining time,}

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.560
even if it meant the annihilation of all mankind as a result. {...wouldn't matter if, in the end, all of mankind was going to be destroyed.} {didn't care if it meant the dest of humanity} {it wouldn't matter even if mankind were annihilated}

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.210
But, you called your grandfather.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.530
I thought you were giving in already.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.780
So I came by to get her.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.720
You're wrong! You really think I was giving in?!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.580
We were just going to rest a little bit,
 borrow some money, and after that...

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.450
What's <i>wrong</i>  with you?

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.750
If that's true, you don't have any time to sit around eating ramen.{this is no time 2b} {u shouldn't be eating ramen here, should you?} {sb ok}

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.290
This is Enomoto. Puppy is headed your way.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.120
His intention is to recover Alice.
All troops are to stand by. {all members/troops stand by}

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.080
Do <i>not</i>  interfere with Puppy.
Discontinue all of Alice's treatments.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.390
Hey, wait a...

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.460
Hurry up and get out of here.
 I'll give you 30 minutes.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.650
Once 30 minutes go by,
we'll pursue you for real.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.400
This is Enomoto. Disregard the previous orders.{355}

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.360
What?! But we've already begun to-

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.480
I was joking.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.620
I want to know...

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.660
...the truth.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.070
Hey, why are you people always like that?

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.700
Imagine this.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:26.070
The Earth is being invaded by UFOs.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:30.280
Iriya is the sole pilot of the fighter that can counter them.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:34.920
And if she's defeated in the upcoming final battle,

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.920
all of humanity will be destroyed. {annihilated}

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.630
If I told you that, would you believe me? {if this is what I told you, would u believe it}

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.810
Or how about this? Keep it between us, okay?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.560
The war that Iriya is fighting in
 is just an ordinary human war. {inevitably breaks out between countries}

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.450
{Lunar: War-driven efforts have produced a device that can control gravity... }The root cause of this war was the invention of a gravity control device. {AnY-Spork: gc device was invented unexpectedly due to the war} {Ayu definitely had the best TL for this little technobabble section.}

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:00.200
And in order to make it work, 
a special kind of ESP is needed.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.570
Only a child whose nervous system has
 undergone special treatment can operate it.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.940
All the hue and cry about UFOs is just a means to an end;

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.720
to make the kids believe that 
they aren't killing humans, {UFO fairy tale = smoke and mirrors} {UFOs & stuff are just an expedient made up to fool the kids / and make them think they kill non-humans - wut} {split}

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.750
we convinced them that their opponents are aliens who've come to invade the Earth.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.590
You can think of it like a game.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.150
A game where you die for real
 if you get shot down.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.940
Under that belief, Iriya has shot down
 dozens of enemy pilots just like herself,

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:33.100
and has also killed tens of thousands of civilians in enemy states.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.690
If I told you that, would you believe me?

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.600
I would.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.280
Why? How can you say that?

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.600
Because...

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.160
I don't really hate you.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.290
They're both true.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.960
Technically speaking, we are fighting aliens.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.540
But even in this dire situation,

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.850
some stupid humans continue
 to fight among themselves.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.130
Why?

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.480
Iriya is the only pilot left alive.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.200
If Iriya loses in the final battle...

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.280
...we will perish.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.620
Finish it before it gets cold.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.150
When is the final battle?

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.550
In three days.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.650
Three more days...

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.340
It's all right.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.560
You've got nothing to worry about. {have nothing}

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.520
I'm the one who's going to Hell. {for this ~ (would be too long if I added "for this")}

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.350
Naoyuki? Are you awake?

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.120
What is it?

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.320
The war... is over. {fsc}

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.780
The Self-Defense Force press conference will begin momentarily...

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.280
Cease-fire agreement at last

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.280
I repeat, the Chief Cabinet Secretary announced that a cease-fire agreement has bee-

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.280
{top line} Thorough{detailed} Discussion!! {either "debate" or "discussion" -guu}

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.280
{2nd line} Questioning the
 meaning of the war!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.280
And that's why! It's because of those <i>things</i>, I tell you!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.290
We're receiving images from various locations.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.330
It looks like a cursed video, doesn't it?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.830
We'll continue to follow this story...

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.830
You think normal classes will resume tomorrow?

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.910
I'm tired. I'm heading to bed.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.490
Good night.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.770
The army was able to competently handle each incident as they occurred...

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.500
...and was finally able to locate and capture the base of the opposition forces. {succeeded in gaining control of their counter-strike positions}

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:21.400
The government was then able to restore order to the situation with minimal casualties.{we were able to come back and achieve victory}

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.290
With "minimal casualties"...

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.700
"Slow down on school grounds"

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.840
So starting today, we'll be having normal classes again... {848}

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.080
Sensei!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.630
The unworthy Asaba Naoyuki has returned in shame.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:59.790
I'm terribly sorry to have troubled you.

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.140
Asaba...

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.060
Don't make your parents worry so much.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.150
Yes, sir.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.440
By the way, Asaba...

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.480
Why are you the only one wearing a summer uniform?

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.080
Asaba?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.660
I heard from Sudou that you 
ran away from home. Is that true?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.430
She was <i>really</i>  worried about you.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:33.050
I didn't run away{from home}. Since school was out, 
 I decided to try some "no-budget travel."

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.880
Hey, Asaba.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:35.770
What?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:38.740
I heard that Iriya dumped you. {is that true}

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.800
H-Hey, don't cry. I shouldn't have said that... {949} {I'm sorry, Asaba...}{my bad, Asaba}

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.410
Hey...

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.440
Um, Asaba Naoyuki-kun from Class 2-4...

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:05.980
Guess what? We just received a call for you. {What was that... there's a call for you.}

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.690
It's from that SDF helicopter... {I prefer to think that this administrator is trying to cope with the absurdity of these announcements via humor at this point...}

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:11.940
Hey! What are you doing? 
{Who ARE you guys?}What the hell?! Hey, stop it!

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.050
This is Hagiyama, from the Ground SDF Military Intelligence Section Four.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:18.610
Asaba Naoyuki-kun, attendance seat #1 in Class 2-4.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.950
This is a matter of pressing urgency, 
and your cooperation has become necessary.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.010
We are coming to fetch you immediately. {an escort}

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:29.850
Asaba...

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.060
I'll be back.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.770
Asaba! You'd better come back, or else!

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:52.720
Hurry up and get on!
 We don't have much time!

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.130
O-Okay!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.540
I'm Sakisaka Eri. Nice to meet you... I think. {This is the first time we've met... or is it?}

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.460
Were you sick or injured 
during the school festival?

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.410
Huh?

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.560
Have you ever flown before? {Ayu: Or is this our first time meeting? --wrong; how did they manage to get so many other lines right but mishear "sora tobu" as "soretomo"?}

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.040
N-No.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.870
You'll feel better if you try 
to get some shuteye.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.150
I'll give you some sleeping pills.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.730
Is it that long of a flight?

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:23.110
Our minimum time till landing is about six hours. {estimated landing time is, at minimum}
The destination is still classified.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:25.740
Will she...

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.540
Will Iriya be at the destination?

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.920
Iriya's Sky

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.920
Summer of UFOs

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.150
Probably.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:45.640
That's...

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.560
The aircraft carrier{U.S.S} Ticonderoga.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:08.470
Sorry you had to take such a long trip.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.540
Things look pretty serious.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.850
What? Compared to what's about to happen,

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.600
everything we've been through so far is nothing.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:26.550
Excuse me, but...

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.430
Iriya's refusing to sortie.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.520
At the last minute, she said 
she didn't want to fight anymore.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.750
We're at our wit's end. {credit to AnY-spork for the most accurate and concise line here.}

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.230
In the worst-case scenario,
 she might commit suicide.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:41.130
But why?

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.460
Isn't the war already over?

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.530
Who told you that?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.990
It was on T.V.! {Fox News, they never lie}

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:55.290
What about Iriya? Where is she?

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:58.410
I'm leading you right to her, 
 so hold your horses.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.750
Iriya, Asaba is here.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.350
Come on, stop messing around.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:25.690
How about you, Asaba,
 and I have a little chat?

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.790
To be honest, I can't guarantee your safety.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.360
We'll try our best,
but once you cross that line,

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.080
we might not be able to protect you
 if the shit hits the fan. { a bit of a stretch, but I think it fits a gruff military guy like Enomoto.}

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:17.870
Iriya! {1417}

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:28.210
Iriya! Iriya!

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.040
Divine Grace
 Guaranteed to hit the target
 Certain kill with one blow!
 ~Sonohara Base Commander-in-Chief

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.250
"It's all right" {may be the first time I've used an an5 tag on its own.}

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.670
Iriya. Hey, Iriya?

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:45.850
Do you know...

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.740
...who I am?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.040
Asaba.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.000
Iriya...

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.860
Asaba, why...?

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:10.610
Why... Why... until... until now...

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.760
Why haven't you come back {for me}until now?

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.270
Why...

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:20.170
...did you leave me behind?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:24.190
Do you hate me now?

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.970
Did you leave me...

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:33.780
...because you hated me?

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:38.250
The night was so dark... it was really dark.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.880
I was scared... so scared.

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:44.480
I thought you would come back for me.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:47.090
I waited and waited for such a long time. {and waited}

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:50.700
It was scary and dark.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:55.630
It was so dark and scary... 
thinking that you'd come to hate me.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.590
It was so frightening, and painful...

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:02.100
And then everything went pitch black.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.770
Hey, Iriya.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.700
I'm sorry I such terrible things.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.120
I didn't mean them. {wasn't serious}

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.320
I was so upset that I couldn't do anything for you.{s?} I was furious at myself.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.890
I was at the end of my rope,
 so I blurted those things out.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.700
But you know, the truth is...

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.300
Bring it on!

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.590
If you think I'm going to persuade her,
 you're wrong!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.780
I won't let her sortie for you anymore!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.310
Asa... ba.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.700
There's no way I'll let Iriya die!

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:05.960
{As long as Iriya's alive, I don't care about mankind or what happens to it}I'm prepared to let mankind or anything else get destroyed, if it'll keep Iriya alive!

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:09.290
Iriya.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.260
I like you. {love?}

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.250
I've always liked you. {definitely like u}

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.520
Day in, day out, you're all I ever think of.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:27.390
On the days you didn't come to school, 
all I could do was stare at your empty desk.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:32.320
On days you came to school, 
 your presence was enough to make me happy.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.340
Ever since we first met 
at the pool that night, I've always...

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:41.030
From then until now, I've always...

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.330
I have always liked you.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:48.830
And I'll always keep on liking you.

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:54.150
Asaba Naoyuki...

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:59.090
...LOVES IRIYA KANA!!

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:13.980
I finally understand how I feel about you, Asaba.

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.260
That's why it's enough.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:19.910
It's all right. Everything's fine.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:21.780
Iriya?

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.640
I don't care about anyone else, either.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.690
Even if everyone else dies, I won't care.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.560
I will protect no one but you.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:34.350
I'll only fight for you,

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.630
and I'll only die for you.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:37.910
I...

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.760
only need to have you.

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.530
Iriya! {1901}

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.920
Good work on that final push.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:34.260
Man, I never thought it would go <i>this</i>  smoothly.

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:38.570
The whole world should give you a medal.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.560
Well, a lot happened along the way,

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:53.120
but you did a brilliant job at the very end.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.740
Thank you...

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:59.170
...and farewell, Asaba Naoyuki-kun.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.040
{Jeez/Geez... // not exactly fitting the "tough guy just took a dozen rounds" context}Damn it all...

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.760
{Lunar: You kept yourself locked up until the very end. // given the number of totally wrong lines like this, maybe it's better that Lunar dropped the series.} You're a pathetic SOB through and through.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.530
Weren't you going to destroy the world?

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.770
I'm...

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:40.290
I'm glad it was you...

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:43.800
...who killed me in the end.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.990
<i>And then, the Prez came back.{2126} {chairman?}</i>

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:36.600
I can't remember! I can't remember anything!!

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:41.610
Our school nurse, Kurobe-sensei, who'd been on leave since June, resumed her duties.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:46.400
The broken public telephones were replaced with three new ones,

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.870
and Akiho...

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:52.770
I have a right to know too, don't I?

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:04.800
Once the base gets downsized, 
Sonohara is going to become a boring place.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:05.530
I'm home.

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:06.600
Oh, welcome back.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:12.230
<i>Asaba Naoyuki-sama. {ita?}</i>

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:18.120
<i>It's embarrassing, but I have very little experience writing letters.</i>

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:22.020
<i>Even so, I had to write
 this letter no matter what.</i>

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:25.730
<i>I wanted to leave a record of the truth, in writing.</i>

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.960
<i>That's why I didn't sign this envelope.</i>

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:34.160
<i>If you want to know why, it's because my real name isn't Shiina Mayumi.</i>

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:41.080
<i>At the beginning of last year, I was ordered to take part in the Roswell Project.</i>

00:22:41.820 --> 00:22:45.610
<i>At the time, there were only two surviving Black Manta pilots:</i>

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:48.940
<i>Iriya Kana and Erica Proudfoot.</i>

00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:53.100
<i>Their combat prowess was deteriorating, and it became a serious problem.</i>

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:58.180
<i>The only thing that barely made them keep fighting</i>

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:01.360
<i>was their desire to protect each other.</i>

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:07.640
<i>That singular cause was suddenly and
 irreversibly lost in August of last year.</i>

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.070
"The Wild Wild Girl's Adventures Continue"

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:11.890
<i>While returning from a routine patrolling mission,</i>

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:14.790
<i>the engine of Erica's Black Manta 
began to run out of control.</i>

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:18.740
<i>And the only one who could stop her from accelerating{s}</i>

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>was the girl who always went on sorties with her, Iriya.</i>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:26.280
<i>Iriya, having received a command to shoot her down,</i>

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:31.260
<i>chased the ever-accelerating Erica 
around the Earth four times.</i>

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:34.450
<i>The communications from that time period were lost.{s}</i>

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:38.930
<i>But even if they weren't, I wouldn't have had 
the courage to listen to them.</i>

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:47.070
<i>After that, Iriya became deeply autistic. {withdrew into herself}</i>

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:51.300
<i>Whenever she seemed about to recover, 
she would suffer some serious aftereffects.</i>

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:54.300
<i>One of them was missing memories.</i>

00:23:54.300 --> 00:24:01.180
<i>Inside Iriya's mind, she'd already made up a story that she didn't sortie on that day. {wasn't the one who shot Erica down}</i>

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:06.710
<i>She also imagined that she'd become able to perceive Erica's spirit.</i>

00:24:09.710 --> 00:24:14.990
<i>The restoration of Iriya's motivation was our highest priority.</i>

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:20.430
<i>Our job was to find something that Iriya would want to protect.</i>

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:26.900
<i>But on the night{evening} of August 31st, 
Iriya Kana went AWOL from Sonohara base...</i>

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:30.440
<i>...and she encountered you at the Sonohara Junior High Pool.</i>

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:31.170
You're late!

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:35.570
<i>You probably know more about what happened to Iriya after that.</i>

00:24:38.720 --> 00:24:40.220
Hey, you all right?

00:24:40.650 --> 00:24:44.570
<i>The staff who were aware of the circumstances</i>

00:24:40.810 --> 00:24:44.580
Yeah, I'm fine already, so knock it off!

00:24:44.570 --> 00:24:47.170
<i>labeled our next action "Operation Puppy".</i>

00:24:47.170 --> 00:24:50.350
<i>Of course, "Puppy" referred to you.</i>

00:24:50.350 --> 00:24:53.800
<i>You meant the entire world to us.</i>

00:24:56.570 --> 00:24:58.770
Hey, Asaba.

00:24:58.770 --> 00:25:00.330
What?

00:25:00.330 --> 00:25:02.310
I'm sorry about what I did back there.

00:25:02.540 --> 00:25:06.680
I worked so hard to become friends with Iriya, 
but she suddenly disappeared.

00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:12.170
I thought it was either unfair or sad that you had to deal with everything on your own.

00:25:12.170 --> 00:25:13.460
You know...

00:25:13.460 --> 00:25:18.530
It's fine, really. I'll wait until you're 
comfortable enough to talk about it. {tell me when you feel like it}

00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:22.790
<i>Do you hate Enomoto?</i>

00:25:23.170 --> 00:25:27.920
<i>But thinking back on it now,
 I have to wonder if he was the only one</i>

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:33.160
<i>who believed in the importance of
 giving Iriya a "puppy" to the bitter end.</i>

00:25:34.040 --> 00:25:37.660
<i>Even now, I can understand how Enomoto felt.</i>

00:25:38.030 --> 00:25:42.470
<i>Of course, it was all for the sake of 
making Iriya sortie in the final battle.</i>

00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:44.720
<i>I have no intention to deny that.</i>

00:25:45.260 --> 00:25:47.510
Prez, you're late too!

00:25:47.460 --> 00:25:53.170
<i>However, I simply cannot believe that what Iriya Kana,
 who lived as a pilot of the Black Manta,  {gotta go with Ayu on these three lines, as they're a very tangled web to interpret.}</i>

00:25:51.230 --> 00:25:53.270
Where were you and what were you doing?!

00:25:53.170 --> 00:25:58.720
<i> saw with her eyes, heard with her ears, and felt with her skin at the very end</i>

00:25:53.270 --> 00:25:55.360
What's with you, correspondent Sudou?!

00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:57.240
What did I do all of that work for?

00:25:57.820 --> 00:26:00.700
H-H-Hey, stop that!

00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:04.950
<i>was cheapened or rendered false
 by the sins of those who brought it to her.</i>

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:02.700
It's all your fault in the first place!  What part of "stop" don't you understand?!

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:07.190
Hey, President.

00:26:07.190 --> 00:26:09.210
What is it, Correspondent Asaba?

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:13.170
I've been thinking about the design of the "Mystery Circle"...

00:26:13.170 --> 00:26:16.760
The design of the "Mystery Circle"? 
What's <i>that</i>  about?

00:26:18.410 --> 00:26:22.120
Weren't we working on the "Mystery Circle"
 joke project today?

00:26:22.120 --> 00:26:24.850
"Farewell US Forces", "Farewell Foo Fighters",

00:26:24.850 --> 00:26:27.630
"Riddle{Mystery lol} of the Mystery Circle 
Overlooking Sonohara Base"...

00:26:27.630 --> 00:26:29.940
Wasn't this all <i>your</i>  idea?

00:26:30.170 --> 00:26:34.270
"Mystery Circle"? "Foo Fighters"?

00:26:37.580 --> 00:26:42.010
You're living behind the times!!{I don't remember anything} {OH, COME ON NOW}{can't remember any of them} {at least I think this is "okuretteru" ~Z}

00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:45.700
I'll do it, alone if I have to.

00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:49.730
By "do it," you mean you'll create the "Mystery Circle"?

00:26:49.730 --> 00:26:50.290
Yes.

00:26:50.290 --> 00:26:51.860
Even by yourself?

00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:52.480
Yes.

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:54.070
No matter what?

00:26:54.070 --> 00:26:54.500
Yes.

00:26:57.180 --> 00:26:58.260
Do as you like.

00:26:59.310 --> 00:27:00.440
Yes.

00:27:02.890 --> 00:27:06.790
<i>I truly believe that for Kana-chan,</i>

00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:11.020
<i>"because Asaba is there"
 was more than enough of a reason.</i>

00:27:11.100 --> 00:27:19.060
A crowd of uniforms streamed into the twilight... {fi fo}

00:27:11.100 --> 00:27:19.060
{}Tasogare ni {}nagaredashita {}seifuku no mure ni{}

